From: Omni build harness
Subject: Fix NaX loader build on Bookworm's mingw-w64 12.2 (__faststorefence under -mno-sse)

The NaX loader (src_loader) is compiled as C++ with -mno-sse. On Debian
Bookworm's mingw-w64 (12.2.0), winnt.h pulls in psdk_inc/intrin-impl.h, which
defines __faststorefence() using __builtin_ia32_sfence(). That builtin is
unavailable when -mno-sse is active, so every loader translation unit fails to
compile:

    intrin-impl.h:667:5: error: '__builtin_ia32_sfence' was not declared in
    this scope; did you mean '__builtin_ia32_fnclex'?

NaX's beacon (src_beacon) already avoids this because its Common.h includes
Macros.h (which pre-defines the guard macro) before windows.h. The loader's
Common.h pulls <windows.h> BEFORE <Macros.h>, so the guard arrives too late and
the header still emits its broken inline __faststorefence().

Pre-define the same guard macro intrin-impl.h checks (via __INTRINSIC_PROLOG)
at the very top of src_loader/include/Common.h, before <windows.h>, so the
header skips the definition entirely. Only src_loader is affected; the beacon
build is unchanged.

diff --git a/src_loader/include/Common.h b/src_loader/include/Common.h
index a8e3fe3..906664b 100644
--- a/src_loader/include/Common.h
+++ b/src_loader/include/Common.h
@@ -1,6 +1,18 @@
 #ifndef STARDUST_COMMON_H
 #define STARDUST_COMMON_H
 
+//
+// mingw-w64 intrinsic workaround (Bookworm 12.2 + -mno-sse).
+// winnt.h -> psdk_inc/intrin-impl.h defines __faststorefence() using
+// __builtin_ia32_sfence(), which is unavailable under -mno-sse and breaks the
+// build. Pre-defining this guard (the same macro intrin-impl.h checks via
+// __INTRINSIC_PROLOG) makes it skip that definition entirely. This MUST come
+// before <windows.h> here, since Common.h pulls windows.h before Macros.h.
+//
+#ifndef __INTRINSIC_DEFINED___faststorefence
+#define __INTRINSIC_DEFINED___faststorefence
+#endif
+
 //
 // system headers
 //
